 ## Storage
 
-Sessions live in Postgres ([keep sessions in the database](../adrs/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)).
+Sessions live in a dictionary in each web process. Requests use the shared `sessions` instance in
+[`larder/session_store.py`](../../larder/session_store.py); creating a store per request would discard earlier sessions.
 
-## Shaped by
+## Known limits
 
-- [Keep sessions in the database](../adrs/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)
+- Restarting a process, including on deploy, discards its sessions and logs its members out. Deploy outside opening
+  hours to reduce disruption; members must sign in again afterward.
+- Processes do not share sessions. In 2023, moving to two servers behind a load balancer caused members to be logged
+  out when requests reached the other server; Postgres previously solved this. Use a single web process with this
+  store, or restore shared storage before serving requests from multiple processes.
+- Stored sessions are not automatically evicted. Restarting the process reclaims their memory and requires members
+  to sign in again. The lifetime calculation in `larder/sessions.py` is unchanged.
